{"obs_mqv8p9cw_28942ba8f7a7":{"observation":{"hookType":"session_updated","id":"obs_mqv8p9cw_28942ba8f7a7","raw":{"additions":null,"deletions":null,"files":null,"parentID":"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI","title":"Fix pg_episodic_store bugs (@languages/python-pro subagent)"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae60061ffewNVfdg0kVd2yhG","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:37.759Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8p9cx_0373b0f74f45":{"observation":{"hookType":"prompt_submit","id":"obs_mqv8p9cx_0373b0f74f45","raw":{"agent":"languages/python-pro","files":[],"model":{"modelID":"big-pickle","providerID":"opencode"},"parts_summary":["text"],"prompt":"Fix 2 critical bugs in /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py. Read the file first.\n\n**Bug 1: UUID-zero sentinel (lines ~159-183)**\n`store_decision_episode()` silently returns `uuid.UUID(int=0)` (all-zeros) when `self._pool` is None. Since `connect()` is a no-op (`pass`), `_pool` is always None. Fix: Raise `RuntimeError` immediately:\n```python\nif not self._pool:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"PgEpisodicStore: PostgreSQL pool not initialized — call connect() with a real DSN\")\n```\n\n**Bug 2: retrieve_similar ignores query_text (lines ~60-62)**\nWhen `embedding is None` and `query_text` is provided, the code falls through to `get_memories()` sorted by recency, completely ignoring `query_text`. Fix: Add a branch for the `embedding is None` case that uses `search_memory` when `query_text` is provided:\n```python\nif embedding is None:\n    if query_text:\n        results = search_memory(CATEGORY, query_text, n_results=top_k, filter_metadata={\"archived\": \"False\"})\n        processed = []\n        for r in results:\n            sim = 1.0 - r.get(\"distance\", 0.0)\n            if sim < min_score:\n                continue\n            metadata = r.get(\"metadata\", {})\n            processed.append({\n                \"id\": r[\"id\"],\n                \"type\": metadata.get(\"type\", \"\"),\n                \"summary\": metadata.get(\"summary\", \"\"),\n                \"raw_text\": metadata.get(\"raw_text\", \"\"),\n                \"importance\": float(metadata.get(\"importance\", 1.0)),\n                \"recall_count\": int(metadata.get(\"recall_count\", 0)),\n                \"last_recalled\": metadata.get(\"last_recalled\", None),\n                \"timestamp\": metadata.get(\"timestamp\", \"\"),\n                \"decay_score\": float(metadata.get(\"decay_score\", 1.0)),\n                \"archived\": metadata.get(\"archived\", \"False\") == \"True\",\n                \"similarity\": sim,\n            })\n        return processed\n    else:\n        memories = get_memories(CATEGORY, n_results=max(50, top_k * 10))\n        # rest of existing code...\n```\n\nAlso need to add `search_memory` to the import line (currently it's not imported after a prior edit):\n```python\nfrom agentmemory import create_memory, get_memories, get_memory, search_memory, update_memory\n```\n\nReturn a summary of every change.","variant":null},"sessionId":"ses_0fae60061ffewNVfdg0kVd2yhG","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:37.761Z","userPrompt":"Fix 2 critical bugs in /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py. Read the file first.\n\n**Bug 1: UUID-zero sentinel (lines ~159-183)**\n`store_decision_episode()` silently returns `uuid.UUID(int=0)` (all-zeros) when `self._pool` is None. Since `connect()` is a no-op (`pass`), `_pool` is always None. Fix: Raise `RuntimeError` immediately:\n```python\nif not self._pool:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"PgEpisodicStore: PostgreSQL pool not initialized — call connect() with a real DSN\")\n```\n\n**Bug 2: retrieve_similar ignores query_text (lines ~60-62)**\nWhen `embedding is None` and `query_text` is provided, the code falls through to `get_memories()` sorted by recency, completely ignoring `query_text`. Fix: Add a branch for the `embedding is None` case that uses `search_memory` when `query_text` is provided:\n```python\nif embedding is None:\n    if query_text:\n        results = search_memory(CATEGORY, query_text, n_results=top_k, filter_metadata={\"archived\": \"False\"})\n        processed = []\n        for r in results:\n            sim = 1.0 - r.get(\"distance\", 0.0)\n            if sim < min_score:\n                continue\n            metadata = r.get(\"metadata\", {})\n            processed.append({\n                \"id\": r[\"id\"],\n                \"type\": metadata.get(\"type\", \"\"),\n                \"summary\": metadata.get(\"summary\", \"\"),\n                \"raw_text\": metadata.get(\"raw_text\", \"\"),\n                \"importance\": float(metadata.get(\"importance\", 1.0)),\n                \"recall_count\": int(metadata.get(\"recall_count\", 0)),\n                \"last_recalled\": metadata.get(\"last_recalled\", None),\n                \"timestamp\": metadata.get(\"timestamp\", \"\"),\n                \"decay_score\": float(metadata.get(\"decay_score\", 1.0)),\n                \"archived\": metadata.get(\"archived\", \"False\") == \"True\",\n                \"similarity\": sim,\n            })\n        return processed\n    else:\n        memories = get_memories(CATEGORY, n_results=max(50, top_k * 10))\n        # rest of existing code...\n```\n\nAlso need to add `search_memory` to the import line (currently it's not imported after a prior edit):\n```python\nfrom agentmemory import create_memory, get_memories, get_memory, search_memory, update_memory\n```\n\nReturn a summary of every change."},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8p9d9_fb79f6259e0e":{"observation":{"hookType":"session_status","id":"obs_mqv8p9d9_fb79f6259e0e","raw":{"attempt":null,"message":"","status_type":"busy"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae60061ffewNVfdg0kVd2yhG","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:37.772Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8p9da_4d335b7e7176":{"observation":{"hookType":"assistant_message","id":"obs_mqv8p9da_4d335b7e7176","raw":{"cost":0,"duration_ms":null,"error":null,"finish":null,"messageID":"msg_f0519ffad001oEGmjFfpMuB1OJ","mode":"languages/python-pro","modelID":"big-pickle","parentID":"msg_f0519ffa0002oVV5y4gydgW832","providerID":"opencode","tokens":{"cache_read":0,"cache_write":0,"input":0,"output":0,"reasoning":0}},"sessionId":"ses_0fae60061ffewNVfdg0kVd2yhG","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:37.773Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8p9if_9c2394553eb4":{"observation":{"hookType":"session_diff","id":"obs_mqv8p9if_9c2394553eb4","raw":{"additions":0,"deletions":0,"diffs":[],"files":[]},"sessionId":"ses_0fae60061ffewNVfdg0kVd2yhG","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:37.959Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8p9ir_523a1fb408c5":{"observation":{"hookType":"llm_params","id":"obs_mqv8p9ir_523a1fb408c5","raw":{"agent":"languages/python-pro","context_limit":200000,"cost_1k_input":0,"cost_1k_output":0,"max_output_tokens":32000,"model":"opencode/big-pickle","provider_url":"https://opencode.ai/zen/v1"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae60061ffewNVfdg0kVd2yhG","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:37.970Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8pbv6_95f27f59bde1":{"observation":{"hookType":"reasoning","id":"obs_mqv8pbv6_95f27f59bde1","raw":{"messageID":"msg_f0519ffad001oEGmjFfpMuB1OJ","text":""},"sessionId":"ses_0fae60061ffewNVfdg0kVd2yhG","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:41.009Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8pcds_5fa54aa43c9a":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mqv8pcds_5fa54aa43c9a","raw":{"attachments":[],"call_id":"call_00_6aiEbnou1aQpWhe5ICi17176","duration_ms":4,"metadata":{"loaded":[],"preview":"\"\"\"PostgreSQL + pgvector episodic store — Layer 2 memory.\nBacked by agentmemory (ChromaDB) with pgvector-compatible schema semantics.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport uuid\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone, timedelta\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom agentmemory import create_memory, get_memories, get_memory, update_memory\n\n\nCATEGORY = \"episodes\"\n\n\nclass PgEpisodicStore:\n    def __init__(self, dsn: str | None = None) -> None:\n        self._dsn = dsn\n        self._pool = None","truncated":false},"title":"xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py","tool_input":"{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py\"}","tool_name":"read","tool_output":"<path>/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"PostgreSQL + pgvector episodic store — Layer 2 memory.\n2: Backed by agentmemory (ChromaDB) with pgvector-compatible schema semantics.\"\"\"\n3: \n4: from __future__ import annotations\n5: \n6: import json\n7: import uuid\n8: from datetime import datetime, timezone, timedelta\n9: from typing import Any\n10: \n11: from agentmemory import create_memory, get_memories, get_memory, update_memory\n12: \n13: \n14: CATEGORY = \"episodes\"\n15: \n16: \n17: class PgEpisodicStore:\n18:     def __init__(self, dsn: str | None = None) -> None:\n19:         self._dsn = dsn\n20:         self._pool = None\n21: \n22:     async def connect(self) -> None:\n23:         pass\n24: \n25:     async def store_episode(\n26:         self,\n27:         type_: str,\n28:         raw_text: str | None = None,\n29:         summary: str | None = None,\n30:         embedding: list[float] | None = None,\n31:         importance: float = 1.0,\n32:     ) -> str:\n33:         now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n34:         memory_id = str(uuid.uuid4())\n35:         m = {\n36:             \"type\": type_,\n37:             \"raw_text\": raw_text or \"\",\n38:             \"summary\": summary or \"\",\n39:             \"importance\": str(importance),\n40:             \"recall_count\": \"0\",\n41:             \"last_recalled\": \"\",\n42:             \"archived\": \"False\",\n43:             \"timestamp\": now.isoformat(),\n44:         }\n45:         create_memory(\n46:             CATEGORY,\n47:             raw_text or summary or \"\",\n48:             id=memory_id,\n49:             metadata=m,\n50:         )\n51:         return memory_id\n52: \n53:     async def retrieve_similar(\n54:         self,\n55:         embedding: list[float] | None = None,\n56:         query_text: str | None = None,\n57:         top_k: int = 5,\n58:         min_score: float = 0.0,\n59:     ) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n60:         if embedding is None:\n61:             if query_text:\n62:                 results = search_memory(CATEGORY, query_text, n_results=top_k, filter_metadata={\"archived\": \"False\"})\n63:                 processed = []\n64:                 for r in results:\n65:                     dist = r.get(\"distance\", 1.0)\n66:                     sim = 1.0 - dist\n67:                     if sim < min_score:\n68:                         continue\n69:                     processed.append({\n70:                         \"id\": r[\"id\"],\n71:                         \"timestamp\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"timestamp\", \"\"),\n72:                         \"type\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"type\", \"\"),\n73:                         \"raw_text\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"raw_text\", \"\"),\n74:                         \"summary\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"summary\", \"\"),\n75:                         \"embedding\": r.get(\"embedding\"),\n76:                         \"importance\": float(r[\"metadata\"].get(\"importance\", 1.0)),\n77:                         \"recall_count\": int(r[\"metadata\"].get(\"recall_count\", 0)),\n78:                         \"last_recalled\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"last_recalled\", None),\n79:                         \"decay_score\": float(r[\"metadata\"].get(\"decay_score\", 1.0)),\n80:                         \"archived\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"archived\", \"False\") == \"True\",\n81:                         \"similarity\": sim,\n82:                     })\n83:                 return processed\n84:             memories = get_memories(CATEGORY, n_results=max(50, top_k * 10))\n85:             return [\n86:                 {\n87:                     \"id\": r[\"id\"],\n88:                     \"timestamp\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"timestamp\", \"\"),\n89:                     \"type\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"type\", \"\"),\n90:                     \"raw_text\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"raw_text\", \"\"),\n91:                     \"summary\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"summary\", \"\"),\n92:                     \"embedding\": r.get(\"embedding\"),\n93:                     \"importance\": float(r[\"metadata\"].get(\"importance\", 1.0)),\n94:                     \"recall_count\": int(r[\"metadata\"].get(\"recall_count\", 0)),\n95:                     \"last_recalled\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"last_recalled\", None),\n96:                     \"decay_score\": float(r[\"metadata\"].get(\"decay_score\", 1.0)),\n97:                     \"archived\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"archived\", \"False\") == \"True\",\n98:                     \"similarity\": 1.0,\n99:                 }\n100:                 for r in sorted(memories, key=lambda m: m.get(\"metadata\", {}).get(\"created_at\", \"\"), reverse=True)[:top_k]\n101:             ]\n102:         search_query = query_text or ''\n103:         results = search_memory(CATEGORY, search_query, n_results=top_k, filter_metadata={\"archived\": \"False\"})\n104:         processed = []\n105:         for r in results:\n106:             dist = r.get(\"distance\", 1.0)\n107:             sim = 1.0 - dist\n108:             if sim < min_score:\n109:                 continue\n110:             processed.append({\n111:                 \"id\": r[\"id\"],\n112:                 \"timestamp\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"timestamp\", \"\"),\n113:                 \"type\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"type\", \"\"),\n114:                 \"raw_text\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"raw_text\", \"\"),\n115:                 \"summary\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"summary\", \"\"),\n116:                 \"embedding\": r.get(\"embedding\"),\n117:                 \"importance\": float(r[\"metadata\"].get(\"importance\", 1.0)),\n118:                 \"recall_count\": int(r[\"metadata\"].get(\"recall_count\", 0)),\n119:                 \"last_recalled\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"last_recalled\", None),\n120:                 \"decay_score\": float(r[\"metadata\"].get(\"decay_score\", 1.0)),\n121:                 \"archived\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"archived\", \"False\") == \"True\",\n122:                 \"similarity\": sim,\n123:             })\n124:         return processed\n125: \n126:     async def bump_recall(self, id: str) -> None:\n127:         mem = self._get_memory_by_id(id)\n128:         if not mem:\n129:             return\n130:         meta = dict(mem[\"metadata\"])\n131:         rc = int(meta.get(\"recall_count\", 0)) + 1\n132:         meta[\"recall_count\"] = str(rc)\n133:         meta[\"last_recalled\"] = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n134:         update_memory(CATEGORY, id, metadata=meta)\n135: \n136:     async def list_recent(self, hours: int = 24) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n137:         cutoff = datetime.now(timezone.utc) - timedelta(hours=hours)\n138:         all_mem = get_memories(CATEGORY, n_results=5000)\n139:         results = []\n140:         for r in all_mem:\n141:             ts_str = r[\"metadata\"].get(\"timestamp\", \"\")\n142:             try:\n143:                 ts = datetime.fromisoformat(ts_str)\n144:             except Exception:\n145:                 continue\n146:             if ts < cutoff:\n147:                 continue\n148:             results.append({\n149:                 \"id\": r[\"id\"],\n150:                 \"timestamp\": ts_str,\n151:                 \"type\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"type\", \"\"),\n152:                 \"raw_text\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"raw_text\", \"\"),\n153:                 \"summary\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"summary\", \"\"),\n154:                 \"importance\": float(r[\"metadata\"].get(\"importance\", 1.0)),\n155:                 \"recall_count\": int(r[\"metadata\"].get(\"recall_count\", 0)),\n156:                 \"last_recalled\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"last_recalled\", None),\n157:                 \"decay_score\": float(r[\"metadata\"].get(\"decay_score\", 1.0)),\n158:                 \"archived\": r[\"metadata\"].get(\"archived\", \"False\") == \"True\",\n159:             })\n160:         results.sort(key=lambda x: x[\"timestamp\"], reverse=True)\n161:         return results\n162: \n163:     async def execute(self, query: str, *args: Any) -> str:\n164:         raise NotImplementedError(\"execute() stub removed — use store_episode or direct agentmemory calls\")\n165: \n166:     async def fetchval(self, query: str, *args: Any) -> Any:\n167:         raise NotImplementedError(\"fetchval() stub removed — use agentmemory API directly\")\n168: \n169:     def _get_memory_by_id(self, id: str) -> dict | None:\n170:         return get_memory(CATEGORY, id)\n171: \n172:     async"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae60061ffewNVfdg0kVd2yhG","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:41.678Z","toolInput":"{\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py\"}","toolName":"read","toolOutput":"<path>/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"PostgreSQL + pgvector episodic store — Layer 2 memory.\n2: Backed by agentmemory (ChromaDB) with pgvector-compatible schema semantics.\"\"\"\n3: \n4: from __future__ import annotations\n5: \n6: import json\n7: import uuid\n8: from datetime import datetime, timezone, timedelta\n9: from typing import Any\n10: \n11: from agentmemory import create_memory, get_memories, get_memory, update_memory\n12: \n13: \n14: CATEGORY = \"episodes\"\n15: \n16: \n17: class PgEpisodicStore:\n18:     def __init__(self, dsn: str | None = None) -> None:\n19:         self._dsn = dsn\n20:         self._pool = None\n21: \n22:     async def connect(self) -> None:\n23:         pass\n24: \n25:     async def store_episode(\n26:         self,\n27:         type_: str,\n28:         raw_text: str | None = None,\n29:         summary: str | None = None,\n30:         embedding: list[float] | None = None,\n31:         importance: float = 1.0,\n32:     ) -> str:\n33:         now = datetime.now(timezone.utc